## diff_bot_sim
### Initial setup
1. First setup was to have a simple urdf, bring it up in rviz. Two trolley wheels and one castor wheel.
2. Need robot_state_publisher to publish the /robot_description. Rviz wont visualize movable joints with just robot state publisher. We need something that publishes the joint states as well.
3. This is acheived by starting the joint_state_publisher node. You do need the joint_state_publisher_gui to control the joints and see them reflecting in rviz.
4. Finally I added a rviz node to have it start from a certain saved panel state.

### Inertial value addition
1. Inertial values are added to the robot

### Sensor addition without gazebo
1. Odom sensor and lidar are the only two gazebo sensors added 
## Bring up in gazebo
1. Bring up in gazebo requires "gz_sim.launch.py" with a world file. 
2. It also requires "create" executabel in "ros_gz_sim" package to spawn in gazebo
3. "gz_ros_bridge" is required to convert the ign topics in ros2 topics
4. AppendEnvironmentVariable is required to ensure available of models and world files in ro2 environment

## Mapping setup
1. Mapper params file is added in config folder and can be configured easily
2. Mapping is run using "online_async_launch.py" launch file
3. For mapping to work, we need a transform from map to odom

## Navigation setup
1. Run "bringup_launch.py" launch file. Add the nav2_params as one parameter. 
2. It is important to add some value to the map file. Otherwise it will fail to run. Even if there isnt an actual file, dont leave this parameter blank
3. We might need to write a remapper script that would convert the cmd_vel topic to our bot topic. If you havent changed your vel topic name, then this is not required. 

